      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/17-rainbow-fishes-and-co/melanotaenia-australis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Melanotaenia australis is a rainbowfish that reaches a maximum length of about 11 cm. It has long been confused in the hobby with the dwarf rainbowfish, Melanotaenia maccullochi.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/17-rainbow-fishes-and-co/melanotaenia-australis-2/",
      "html": "<p>This species is available both as imports from Indonesia (bred fish) and as German-bred fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/17-rainbow-fishes-and-co/melanotaenia-australis-2/",
      "html": "<p>M. australis is distributed in northern Australia. It was considered a subspecies of M. splendida for a long time. The variety with pretty red fins that is common in the hobby currently looks most similar to the form from the Sale River in the Kimberley region, state of Western Australia.</p>"
    }
